--TEST--
A conversion with `as int` in a `try`, whose value comes from a call that can throw, gives `null` for an error from the call as well — `rule:expressions/a-cheaper-form-with-the-same-result-is-compiled-or-named`
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Convert {
    // `read` throws an error for an empty string.
    public static function read(string $s): mixed {
        if ($s == "") {
            throw new RuntimeError("empty");
        }
        return $s;
    }

    public static function toInt(string $s): ?int {
        ?int $v = 0;
        try {
            $v = Convert::read($s) as int;
        } catch (RuntimeError) {
            $v = null;
        }
        return $v;
    }
}

// `"42"` converts. `"abc"` does not convert, and `""` makes `read` throw. Both give `null`.
array<string> $inputs = ["42", "abc", ""];
foreach ($inputs as string $s) {
    echo Core\Json::encode(Convert::toInt($s)), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
42
null
null
